Article 4 (Timing of Public Disclosure of Management Information, etc.)
(1) A City/Do Institute shall publicly disclose the matters specified in the subparagraphs of Article 35 (1) of the Act at the following times:
1. Matters under Article 35 (1) 1, 3, and 4 of the Act: Within 30 days after approval by the Mayor/Do Governor under Article 27 (1) of the Act;
2. Matters under Article 35 (1) 2 and 6 of the Act: Within 30 days after approval by the Mayor/Do Governor under Article 27 (3) of the Act;
3. Matters under Article 35 (1) 5 and 7 of the Act: Within 30 days after notification under Article 34 (5) of the Act;
4. Matters under Article 35 (1) 8 of the Act: Immediately whenever the relevant cause arises.
(2) When disclosing matters under paragraph (1), data for the most recent five years shall be disclosed. Provided, where data for the most recent five years are unavailable or cannot be disclosed, data for the period for which they can be obtained shall be disclosed, and the reasons shall be stated for any period for which data cannot be obtained.
